Keeping the previous beta on a failed fit is a trade-off stated here as one, not as an unqualified safeguard: it keeps the engine from trading on a garbage regression, but a beta that goes stale across several consecutive failed fits is itself a source of model drift — it was fitted on a window that no longer exists and may no longer describe the current relationship between the signal and the confounds. GetFailStreak() exists specifically so a caller does not have to treat "has a beta" and "has a
current
beta" as the same thing; the Expert Advisor section below shows it gating new entries.
