Everything about when a bar is scored and when it is learned from comes down to one fixed rule, stated here in MQL5's own terms rather than a paraphrase of them: in this codebase, shift 1 is the last
closed
bar and shift 0 is the bar still forming. Every call in this project that reads market data uses shift 1 — shift 0 is never read, because a forming bar's close is not yet final. OnTick() runs once per new bar and, for the closed bar t at shift 1, does exactly two things in this order:
