The synthetic dataset used for the first check below is built from a known, injected relationship: 1,400 bars where the raw signal is a sum of a decaying oscillatory term plus a known multiple of a volatility-like series and a trend-slope-like series plus idiosyncratic noise. Because the volatility and trend-slope exposure is injected on purpose and its coefficients are known, the before/after correlation change is checkable against ground truth rather than against an assumption:
